# Secure Spring Boot Backend

Generate complete, production-ready code. No placeholders or wildcard imports.

## pom.xml Dependencies

Include at minimum:
- `spring-boot-starter-web`, `spring-boot-starter-data-jpa`, `spring-boot-starter-security`
- `spring-boot-starter-oauth2-resource-server`, `spring-boot-starter-validation`
- `mapstruct` + `mapstruct-processor` (annotation processor scope)
- BCrypt via Spring Security; virtual threads: `spring.threads.virtual.enabled=true`

## SecurityConfig

```java
@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
@EnableMethodSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {

    @Bean
    SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        CookieCsrfTokenRepository csrfRepo = CookieCsrfTokenRepository.withHttpOnlyFalse();
        csrfRepo.setCookieName("XSRF-TOKEN");
        csrfRepo.setHeaderName("X-XSRF-TOKEN");
        http
            .csrf(csrf -> csrf
                .csrfTokenRepository(csrfRepo)
                .csrfTokenRequestHandler(new CsrfTokenRequestAttributeHandler()))
            .cors(cors -> cors.configurationSource(corsConfigurationSource()))
            .sessionManagement(sm -> sm.sessionCreationPolicy(SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS))
            .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
                .requestMatchers("/api/auth/**", "/actuator/health").permitAll()
                .anyRequest().authenticated())
            .oauth2ResourceServer(oauth2 -> oauth2.jwt(Customizer.withDefaults()));
        return http.build();
    }

    @Bean
    CorsConfigurationSource corsConfigurationSource(
            @Value("${app.cors.allowed-origins}") String allowedOrigins) {
        CorsConfiguration config = new CorsConfiguration();
        config.setAllowedOrigins(List.of(allowedOrigins.split(",")));
        config.setAllowedMethods(List.of("GET", "POST", "PUT", "PATCH", "DELETE"));
        config.setAllowedHeaders(List.of("Authorization", "Content-Type", "X-XSRF-TOKEN"));
        config.setAllowCredentials(true);
        UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource source = new UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource();
        source.registerCorsConfiguration("/api/**", config);
        return source;
    }
}
```

- Secrets via `@Value("${...}")` or env vars — never hardcode.
- Passwords: BCrypt with strength 12+.
- Auth/session cookies: `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite=Strict`. CSRF uses `CookieCsrfTokenRepository` (token cookie readable by SPA for `X-XSRF-TOKEN` header).

## CRUD Layer (User Example)

- **Entity + Repository**: Spring Data JPA; parameterized queries only.
- **DTOs**: MapStruct mappers; never expose entities from controllers.
- **UserService**: `@Transactional` read/write methods; paginate with `Pageable` / return `Page<UserDto>` or `Slice<UserDto>`.
- **UserController**: `@Valid` on request bodies; `@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")` on mutating endpoints.

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/users")
@PreAuthorize("hasRole('USER')")
public class UserController {

    @GetMapping
    public Page<UserResponse> list(Pageable pageable) {
        return userService.findAll(pageable);
    }

    @PostMapping
    @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
    public ResponseEntity<UserResponse> create(@Valid @RequestBody CreateUserRequest request) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(userService.create(request));
    }
}
```

## Global Error Handling

Use `@RestControllerAdvice` with handlers for `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, `AccessDeniedException`, and domain exceptions. Return structured JSON (timestamp, status, message, field errors).

## Checklist

- [ ] RBAC via `@PreAuthorize` on controllers and sensitive service methods
- [ ] All DTOs validated with `jakarta.validation.constraints`
- [ ] Pagination for list endpoints (`Pageable`)
- [ ] MapStruct for entity ↔ DTO mapping
- [ ] Redis/Hazelcast caching for frequent reads when applicable
